course: dictionary
lesson: 5406
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same little word can mean different things in different places. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning it has. Here the word is «la».
explain: In music, la is a note. Singers climb the scale: do, re, mi, fa, so, la, ti, do. La is the sixth note on that scale, and people also sing «la la la» with no real words.
explain: In a news report about a city, LA is short for Los Angeles, a big city in California, USA. The clue is a capital letter place name, and the word is written in capitals.
explain: In French and Spanish, la means "the". In «À la piscine !» the word after la tells you where you are going: the swimming pool. When you see la in front of a noun, check whether it means "the" before you decide on any other meaning.
fact: La is a noun: a music note, the sixth note in do, re, mi, fa, so, la, ti, do.
fact: La can also be written «lah».
fact: LA is short for Los Angeles, a city in California, USA.
fact: «La la la» is a sound people sing without words, and it can show that someone is not listening.
fact: In French and Spanish, la means "the", as in «la main» (hand).
exercise: In do, re, mi, which note comes straight after so? | Ti | *La | Fa
exercise: «À la piscine !» is French for "To the swimming pool!" What does la mean there? | Sixth note | *The | Los Angeles
exercise: In a news report, «LA» is short for which city? | Lagos | *Los Angeles | Paris
test: What does «la la la» mean in a song? | A city in California | *A sound sung with no real words | The word for "the" in French
test: In French, «la main» means what? | *Hand | Night | Music note
exam: Mia reads «New Year's Eve is la Saint-Sylvestre.» What does la most likely mean here? | Sixth note | *The | Los Angeles | Ti
